\section{Where the token comes from}{

A function reads three sources and uses the first one that holds a value.
\enumerate{
\item The \code{token} argument of the function you call.
\item The \code{rlmstudio.token} option, set with \code{\link[base:options]{base::options()}}.
\item The \code{RLMSTUDIO_API_TOKEN} environment variable.
}

When none of the three holds a value, the request carries no \code{Authorization}
header. A source that is \code{NULL} or an empty string counts as unset.
