\section{Keeping the token out of your output}{

The header is set with \code{\link[httr2:req_auth_bearer_token]{httr2::req_auth_bearer_token()}}, which marks it as
redacted. Printing a request shows \verb{<REDACTED>} in place of the value, and
the abort message of a failed call never carries the value.
}

\section{When the server rejects the call}{

A response with HTTP status 401 or 403 aborts with a condition of class
\code{rlmstudio_api_error}, described in \link{rlmstudio-conditions}. If the request
carried no token, the message tells you to set \code{RLMSTUDIO_API_TOKEN} or to
pass \code{token}. If the request carried a token, the message tells you that the
server rejected it.
}

